  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Break Barriers to Let Women Avail Business in the Tourism Industry</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to address the significant gender gap in Sri Lanka&#x2019;s tourism sector, particularly within the tour guiding profession, by increasing the engagement through building competencies of young women from rural and plantation communities in Nuwara Eliya District. Although tourism is one of Sri Lanka&#x2019;s key economic sectors, women remain significantly underrepresented, accounting for less than 10% of registered tour guides nationally. Women also continue to face barriers such as socio-cultural stigma, safety concerns, limited access to professional training, and restricted employment opportunities within the tourism industry. These challenges are more severe among plantation and rural communities where young women have limited exposure to tourism-related career pathways despite living in a district with strong tourism potential.</narrative>
  </description>
